From a5c7cbeb837d9b55503857806bba540429ba16eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@st.com>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 11:15:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 502/572] fix(st-bsec): use BIT_32 in otp_bit_mask

The function returns an uint32_t, and uses 32bit parameter, it is then
better to use BIT_32 (over BIT and then BIT_64) in otp_bit_mask.

This also corrects the following clang warning:
drivers/st/bsec/bsec3.c:45:9: warning: implicit conversion loses integer
 precision: 'uint64_t' (aka 'unsigned long') to 'uint32_t'
      (aka 'unsigned int') [-Wshorten-64-to-32]
   45 |         return BIT(otp & BSEC_OTP_MASK);
      |         ~~~~~~ ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git bbdd81f5658e36ce158411ae93c018ac9c177552 fix(st-bsec): use BIT_32 in otp_bit_mask]
Change-Id: I8fadd2ad0ed225744b819c127d10ac39e84fcdfd
Signed-off-by: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/572142
Reviewed-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Tested-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
---
 drivers/st/bsec/bsec3.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/st/bsec/bsec3.c b/drivers/st/bsec/bsec3.c
index c4feb8bc7f..14b21a3d1e 100644
--- a/drivers/st/bsec/bsec3.c
+++ b/drivers/st/bsec/bsec3.c
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 /*
- * Copyright (c) 2024-2025, STMicroelectronics - All Rights Reserved
+ * Copyright (c) 2024-2026, STMicroelectronics - All Rights Reserved
  *
  * SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
  */
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@ static uint32_t otp_bank(uint32_t otp)
 
 static uint32_t otp_bit_mask(uint32_t otp)
 {
-	return BIT(otp & BSEC_OTP_MASK);
+	return BIT_32(otp & BSEC_OTP_MASK);
 }
 
